#: ../../source/minimatch_README.md:153
msgid "Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/minimatch_README.md:155
msgid "All options are `false` by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/minimatch_README.md:157
msgid "debug"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/minimatch_README.md:159
msgid "Dump a ton of stuff to stderr."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/minimatch_README.md:161
msgid "nobrace"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/minimatch_README.md:163
#, python-brace-format
msgid "Do not expand `{a,b}` and `{1..3}` brace sets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/minimatch_README.md:165
msgid "noglobstar"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/minimatch_README.md:167
msgid "Disable `**` matching against multiple folder names."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/minimatch_README.md:169
msgid "dot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/minimatch_README.md:171
msgid ""
"Allow patterns to match filenames starting with a period, even if the "
"pattern does not explicitly have a period in that spot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/minimatch_README.md:174
msgid ""
"Note that by default, `a/**/b` will **not** match `a/.d/b`, unless `dot` "
"is set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/minimatch_README.md:177
msgid "noext"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/minimatch_README.md:179
msgid "Disable \"extglob\" style patterns like `+(a|b)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/minimatch_README.md:181
msgid "nocase"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/minimatch_README.md:183
msgid "Perform a case-insensitive match."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/minimatch_README.md:185
msgid "nonull"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/minimatch_README.md:187
msgid ""
"When a match is not found by `minimatch.match`, return a list containing "
"the pattern itself if this option is set.  When not set, an empty list is"
" returned if there are no matches."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/minimatch_README.md:191
msgid "matchBase"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/minimatch_README.md:193
msgid ""
"If set, then patterns without slashes will be matched against the "
"basename of the path if it contains slashes.  For example, `a?b` would "
"match the path `/xyz/123/acb`, but not `/xyz/acb/123`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/minimatch_README.md:197
msgid "nocomment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/minimatch_README.md:199
msgid ""
"Suppress the behavior of treating `#` at the start of a pattern as a "
"comment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/minimatch_README.md:202
msgid "nonegate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/minimatch_README.md:204
msgid "Suppress the behavior of treating a leading `!` character as negation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/minimatch_README.md:206
msgid "flipNegate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/minimatch_README.md:208
msgid ""
"Returns from negate expressions the same as if they were not negated. "
"(Ie, true on a hit, false on a miss.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/minimatch_README.md:211
msgid "partial"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/minimatch_README.md:213
msgid ""
"Compare a partial path to a pattern.  As long as the parts of the path "
"that are present are not contradicted by the pattern, it will be treated "
"as a match.  This is useful in applications where you're walking through "
"a folder structure, and don't yet have the full path, but want to ensure "
"that you do not walk down paths that can never be a match."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/minimatch_README.md:219
msgid "For example,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/minimatch_README.md:227
msgid "allowWindowsEscape"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/minimatch_README.md:229
msgid ""
"Windows path separator `\\` is by default converted to `/`, which "
"prohibits the usage of `\\` as a escape character. This flag skips that "
"behavior and allows using the escape character."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/minimatch_README.md:233
msgid "Comparisons to other fnmatch/glob implementations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/minimatch_README.md:235
msgid ""
"While strict compliance with the existing standards is a worthwhile goal,"
" some discrepancies exist between minimatch and other implementations, "
"and are intentional."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/minimatch_README.md:239
msgid ""
"If the pattern starts with a `!` character, then it is negated.  Set the "
"`nonegate` flag to suppress this behavior, and treat leading `!` "
"characters normally.  This is perhaps relevant if you wish to start the "
"pattern with a negative extglob pattern like `!(a|B)`.  Multiple `!` "
"characters at the start of a pattern will negate the pattern multiple "
"times."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/minimatch_README.md:246
msgid ""
"If a pattern starts with `#`, then it is treated as a comment, and will "
"not match anything.  Use `\\#` to match a literal `#` at the start of a "
"line, or set the `nocomment` flag to suppress this behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/minimatch_README.md:250
msgid ""
"The double-star character `**` is supported by default, unless the "
"`noglobstar` flag is set.  This is supported in the manner of bsdglob and"
" bash 4.1, where `**` only has special significance if it is the only "
"thing in a path part.  That is, `a/**/b` will match `a/x/y/b`, but "
"`a/**b` will not."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/minimatch_README.md:256
msgid ""
"If an escaped pattern has no matches, and the `nonull` flag is set, then "
"minimatch.match returns the pattern as-provided, rather than interpreting"
" the character escapes.  For example, `minimatch.match([], "
"\"\\\\*a\\\\?\")` will return `\"\\\\*a\\\\?\"` rather than `\"*a?\"`.  "
"This is akin to setting the `nullglob` option in bash, except that it "
"does not resolve escaped pattern characters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/minimatch_README.md:263
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"If brace expansion is not disabled, then it is performed before any other"
" interpretation of the glob pattern.  Thus, a pattern like `+(a|{b),c)}`,"
" which would not be valid in bash or zsh, is expanded **first** into the "
"set of `+(a|b)` and `+(a|c)`, and those patterns are checked for "
"validity.  Since those two are valid, matching proceeds."
msgstr ""

